expected_issues.description:
Potential NPE/behavior masking: `agentsModule` is a required constructor dependency (used for entitlement decisions) but is not validated. If it is accidentally passed as `null`, the code will silently skip the agent entitlement branch (`requestingModule == agentsModule` will always be false) and fall through to `NONE`, which could be hard to debug. Suggest failing fast via `requireNonNull(agentsModule)` and likely also `requireNonNull(entitlementsModule)`/`pluginResolver` for consistency with other params.

```suggestion
        this.pluginResolver = requireNonNull(pluginResolver);
                this.agentsModule = requireNonNull(agentsModule);
                this.entitlementsModule = requireNonNull(entitlementsModule);
```

